    <descript>
      <abstract>The data consists of genetic ISSR band scores. Two sets of trees were sampled for genetic analyses - large trees surviving mountain pine beetle and 'general population' trees that we just a little to small to be attacked that served as a proxy for the population without beetle selection. </abstract>
      <purpose>To assess whether survivors are genetically different than those selected by mountain pine beetle indicating a capacity for adaptation over time to beetle presence and increasing drought</purpose>
    </descript>
